course: dictionary
lesson: 3668
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning the writer means by reading the words around it. Fitness is a good example. «Fitness builds from many small, regular sessions, not from one huge session.» The clues are sessions and building up, so fitness means being healthy and strong in your body.
explain: Now read this: «Two cans means twice the caffeine and more jitters and a bigger crash, not twice the fitness.» The clues are caffeine, jitters and crash, which are all about how a body feels. Try swapping in "being healthy and strong" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Fitness can also mean how suitable someone is for a job, as in «fitness for the job». Each time, ask: what are the clues? If the sentence is about exercise or health, use the body meaning. If it is about a task or a living thing, use another meaning.
fact: Fitness is a noun, and it usually has no plural, so we say fitness, not fitnesses.
fact: «Fitness» means being healthy and strong in your body, especially from exercise.
fact: «Fitness» can also mean how good or suitable someone or something is for a task, as in «fitness for the job».
fact: In biology, «fitness» means how well a living thing survives and has young in its environment.
fact: «Physical fitness» means fitness of the body, and a «fitness test» checks how fit you are.
exercise: «Fitness builds from many small, regular sessions, not from one huge session.» What does fitness mean here? | How good someone is for a job | Being lost in a crowd | A type of football shirt | *Being healthy and strong in your body
exercise: «Top referees run about 10 to 12 km in a match, and have to pass fitness tests.» What is a fitness test? | *A test of how fit and strong a person is | A quiz about the weather | A test of your spelling in class | A test to see how much money you have
exercise: Coach says, «She has the fitness for the job.» What does fitness mean here? | The number of jobs she has had | Her shoe size | Her favourite exercise | *How suitable she is for the job
test: «A console game trains thumbs and quick eyes, but not running, balance, touch on a real ball or fitness.» What does the author mean by fitness here? | A type of game | Playing a game on a console | *Strength and health from real exercise | Having quick eyes
test: «A fit person's pulse may be slower at rest and goes back to normal quickly after a race.» What does this tell us about fitness? | Fit people never get tired | *How fast your body recovers is a good test of fitness | Fit people always have a faster pulse at rest | Fit people never need to rest
exam: In biology, what does «fitness» mean? | How many laps a runner can finish | A list of exercises | How strong a teacher thinks you are | *How well a living thing survives and has young in its environment
